Author: Prasad Shirvalkar <prasad.shirvalkar@ucsf.edu>
Date:   Sat Jun 27 03:33:09 2026 -0700

    CS-4: per-PRO LSB selection precedence + sliding-window overlay + saturation QC
    
    Per-PRO LSB now follows a strict, documented source precedence, and the
    per-PRO transform reuses the CS-1 rating-centered window contract that until
    now had no production caller.
    
    availability.per_pro_lsb(pro_times, native_lsb_series, channel, center_hz, ...):
    for each PRO, stop at the first tier that yields a value —
      1) NATIVE device LSB  — a sensed in-band sample within native_tol_s of the
         rating (the band was actually measured; nothing models better).
      2) DIRECT TD->LSB transform (k=352.62) — ANY TD-bearing recording
         (streaming/montage/survey/snapshot, all 250 Hz TD) overlapping the
         rating: cut the 30 s rating-centered extent via
         analytics.transform_centered_window (clip-don't-slide, 1 s-min,
         fail-closed >10% Missing) and run td_to_lsb at 50% overlap.
      3) PSD->LSB BRIDGE (CS-3, k~=73.63) — ONLY a PSD-only patient-triggered
         snapshot event, ONLY inside [LSB_VALIDATED_HZ_LO, LSB_DEPLOYABLE_HZ_HI].
    Montage/survey TD NEVER uses the bridge (it carries TD -> tier 2; it is the
    bridge's calibration source). Returns per-PRO {t,lsb,tier,center_hz,used_s,
    saturated,reason}; an unmatched PRO returns lsb=None/tier=None honestly.
    
    Sliding-window overlay + saturation QC:
    - analytics.td_transform_band_power gains agg='none' -> per-window band power
      ((W,) scalar center / (W,C) vector), no aggregation, one DSP impl. median of
      agg='none' == agg='median' exactly.
    - availability.per_pro_lsb_overlay: the 50%-overlap per-window LSB trace within
      one PRO's 30 s extent {t_offset_s, lsb, median_lsb, used_s, n_windows,
      n_saturated, saturated, ok, reason}; overlay median == the deployed
      single-value path. Per-window saturation QC vs the +-4000 uV ADC rail
      (PRO_LSB_SATURATION_UV); a saturated/clipped window is flagged and dropped,
      >10% Missing rejects the extent up front.
    - Tier + QC constants: PRO_LSB_TIER_NATIVE/TD/BRIDGE, PRO_LSB_SATURATION_UV.
      Local _missing_per_sample (mirrors bravo_service._missing_time_vector, no
      upward import).
    
    Tests: +8 (precedence native>TD>bridge, montage-TD-never-bridge, bridge
    deployable-band gate, saturation flag+skip, honest unmatched, agg='none'
    shapes+median-consistency, overlay trace+QC, short-extent not-ok). Suite
    227/227.

